    <briefdescription>
<para><ref refid="classA" kindref="compound">A</ref> specialized layout taking care of panel display. </para>    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>The panel layout is specialized in several ways : <itemizedlist>
<listitem>
<para>It only operates on specific widgets (which inherit <ref refid="classQPanel" kindref="compound">QPanel</ref>) </para></listitem>
<listitem>
<para>It can only layout widgets in the viewport margins of a <ref refid="classQEditor" kindref="compound">QEditor</ref> (could work with any QAbstractScrollArea if a single method was made public instead of protected...) so it does not qualify as a &quot;real&quot; layout (contrary to grid/box layouts) </para></listitem>
<listitem>
<para>It positions widgets on the border of the editor in the same way the Border Layout example does (most of the layout code actually comes from there). </para></listitem>
<listitem>
<para>It provides serialization/deserialization of its layout structure </para></listitem>
</itemizedlist>
</para>    </detaileddescription>
